Before we go, I'd like to tell you a little bit about the legendary British ska band, Madness.

01:53:02.110 --> 01:53:05.150
One of the early pioneers of the London ska revival of 1979,

01:53:05.370 --> 01:53:07.590
along with bands like The Specials and Selector,

01:53:08.050 --> 01:53:10.330
Madness helped bring ska to the attention of the mainstream,

01:53:10.550 --> 01:53:12.630
and their music achieved what many said was impossible,

01:53:12.810 --> 01:53:13.670
universal appeal.

01:53:14.170 --> 01:53:16.170
Fans of all ages and musical preferences

01:53:16.170 --> 01:53:17.990
were drawn to the band's infectious pop sound

01:53:17.990 --> 01:53:20.130
by songs like Our House, One Step Beyond,

01:53:20.310 --> 01:53:22.850
Grey Day, My Girl, It Must Be Love, and many more.

01:53:23.050 --> 01:53:25.410
The departure of keyboardist Mike Barson in 1983

01:53:25.410 --> 01:53:27.090
was the beginning of the end for the band,

01:53:27.170 --> 01:53:29.190
and they broke up a few years later in 1986,

01:53:29.190 --> 01:53:29.910
Although arena.

01:53:30.000 --> 01:53:34.330
reincarnation of sorts called The Madness carried on for a little longer and there were offshoots

